{"campaign_batch_id": "cmp_block27_e5_shuffle", "disposition": "quarantined", "entry_count": 20, "evidence_ids": [], "experiment_ids": [], "fingerprint": "1c4aef79b2a38004", "first_exp_num": 571, "last_exp_num": 590, "phase": "block27", "provenance": {"artifact_completeness": "partial", "gate_binding": false, "launch_method": "direct_ssh", "limitations": ["Runs bypassed authorize-run and have no immutable gated-experiment binding.", "Per-run config hashes and GPU-sampling provenance are not captured per arm.", "Arm-level val_bpb, step count and median MFU ARE captured, and every arm was screened on the step-count/MFU signature before entering an aggregate."], "run_records_complete": false}, "recorded_at": "2026-07-31T04:20:00Z", "recorded_by": "block27-backfill", "run_ids": [], "source_path": "campaign_log.jsonl", "source_sha256": "8d3194862f4e33f4443a4c185681dd631002fb630d0b9cfa0ec9a7a01ef60a24", "summary": "E5 per-epoch row-group data shuffling, launched on a deliberately different axis after E1/E2/E3 all failed. Verdict NULL at clean n=10, zero quarantines: RAW +0.000149, INTRINSIC +0.000129, 4/10 negative, t=+0.32, 5% of gate. Runtime cost VERIFIED rather than assumed free: 2019 vs 2018 mean steps, -0.03%.", "tags": ["e5", "data_ordering", "null", "different_axis"]}
{"campaign_batch_id": "cmp_block28_e6_sparsegrad", "disposition": "quarantined", "entry_count": 10, "evidence_ids": [], "experiment_ids": [], "fingerprint": "1e1c14186097308f", "first_exp_num": 591, "last_exp_num": 600, "phase": "block28", "provenance": {"artifact_completeness": "partial", "gate_binding": false, "launch_method": "direct_ssh", "limitations": ["Runs bypassed authorize-run and have no immutable gated-experiment binding.", "Round stopped at 5 of 10 preregistered pairs by its own trap-check, so this is a throughput verdict and NOT a val_bpb endpoint; no adoption claim is possible from it."], "run_records_complete": false}, "recorded_at": "2026-07-31T06:00:00Z", "recorded_by": "block28-trapcheck", "run_ids": [], "source_path": "campaign_log.jsonl", "source_sha256": "f366e05987b136469c4ae232990c06ac0e36804105386cd38271f4d04247d41c", "summary": "E6 NGRAM_SPARSE_GRAD sparse gather/scatter for the hashed n-gram value embeddings. KILLED at the preregistered batch-1 trap-check, and killed in the OPPOSITE direction to the prediction: 1779 vs 2016 mean steps, -11.79% steps = +13.37% step time, 5/5 pairs against, every treatment arm below every control arm. The registered prediction was -9.3% step time and RAW -0.0058. The preregistered expected failure mode was named before launch and is what happened: the custom_op boundary blocks inductor epilogue fusion around the n-gram path and the lost fusion costs more than the removed fills. Seventh proposal killed by the compiled-baseline rule. SECONDARY, and unplanned: the token law predicts +0.00753 val_bpb from the lost tokens alone and the observed RAW delta is +0.00841, so the damage is throughput-mediated to within 12% and the intrinsic residual is only +0.0009 -- an independent out-of-sample check of the token law at a 3x larger throughput perturbation than any prior test.", "tags": ["e6", "sparse_grad", "throughput", "trap_check_kill", "compiled_baseline_rule"]}
{"campaign_batch_id": "cmp_block29_e7_fillflood", "disposition": "quarantined", "entry_count": 16, "evidence_ids": [], "experiment_ids": [], "fingerprint": "b302473fb19fc669", "first_exp_num": 601, "last_exp_num": 616, "phase": "block29", "provenance": {"artifact_completeness": "partial", "gate_binding": false, "launch_method": "direct_ssh", "limitations": ["Runs bypassed authorize-run and have no immutable gated-experiment binding.", "A modified train.py was uploaded to the host while this tranche was in flight. All 16 arms were then PROVEN to have loaded the correct source by grepping for a token only the new source emits (TNGRAM_SHARED); every arm returned 0. The provenance is therefore established by direct observation rather than by timestamp inference, but the incident is recorded here because the check, not the process, is what saved it.", "mult=256 is a different operating point with no registered baseline, so nothing in this round is adoptable; it is a mechanism test only."], "run_records_complete": false}, "recorded_at": "2026-07-31T06:45:00Z", "recorded_by": "block29", "run_ids": [], "source_path": "campaign_log.jsonl", "source_sha256": "09d2561cda832e2ffd1288ad6eb769e7699fea8f41293bb877638192cde71210", "summary": "E7 2x2 NGRAM_TABLE_MULT {64,256} x NGRAM_SPARSE_GRAD {0,1}, 4 seeds per cell. DISCRIMINATING TEST REGISTERED BEFORE E6's DATA EXISTED, and CONFIRMED. mech_ngram_dense_embedding_backward_fill_flood predicted the sparse-gradient penalty SHRINKS as tables grow; the rival memory-bandwidth account predicted it is FLAT. Measured penalty in median step time: +19.4 ms (+12.95%) at mult=64, +6.0 ms (+3.22%) at mult=256 -- it fell 3.2x while tables grew 4x. Solving penalty = O - F*(mult/64) on the two points gives a fill cost F=4.47 ms at mult=64 and a custom_op overhead O=23.87 ms, hence break-even near mult=342. That solve is an interpolation, NOT a test (two points, two parameters), and stands as a new prediction for a third multiplier. THE DIRECTION IS NEVERTHELESS CLOSED FOR ADOPTION: mult=256 costs +0.010883 val_bpb against mult=64 (4.2x the gate), so the table size at which sparse gradients pay is far past the quality knee. A real mechanism whose profitable operating point is unreachable.", "tags": ["e7", "ngram", "sparse_grad", "fill_flood", "mechanism_confirmed", "direction_closed"]}
{"campaign_batch_id": "cmp_block30_e8_tngram", "disposition": "quarantined", "entry_count": 15, "evidence_ids": [], "experiment_ids": [], "fingerprint": "91f5d41acfdc5db4", "first_exp_num": 617, "last_exp_num": 631, "phase": "block30", "provenance": {"artifact_completeness": "partial", "gate_binding": false, "launch_method": "direct_ssh", "limitations": ["Runs bypassed authorize-run and have no immutable gated-experiment binding.", "Two of fifteen arms quarantined by a NEW duty-cycle screen (steps divided by TIME_BUDGET/median_step_time). Both had median step time squarely in family and would have PASSED the median-step-time screen adopted one block earlier in paper 028; they lost ~13% of wall clock outside the timed steps. Duty cycle separated cleanly and bimodally: 13 arms at 1.004-1.006 versus 0.870 and 0.893, so no judgement call was involved."], "run_records_complete": false}, "recorded_at": "2026-07-31T07:45:00Z", "recorded_by": "block30", "run_ids": [], "source_path": "campaign_log.jsonl", "source_sha256": "8470e09d586fd8615c33b776c0c8dda0b610a290482fd6c1f3b28d5c6ef35e78", "summary": "E8 TN-gram, three arms x 5 seeds, testing clm_tngram_cp_shared_factors_mechanism -- the only claim in the 123-claim corpus whose recorded scope is literally short_budget_transformer_lm_pretraining. Three arms rather than two, because a two-arm test confounds SHARING with CAPACITY. VERDICT: REJECTED, and the mechanism itself is contradicted. A->B TN-gram vs baseline +0.010517 (4.0 gates WORSE). A->C capacity cut alone +0.007935 (3.0 gates). C->B sharing at matched parameter count +0.002582 (1.0 gate WORSE). So CP sharing across orders is not merely neutral: at matched parameters it is about one gate WORSE than plain independent smaller tables. Roughly 75% of TN-gram's damage is capacity loss and 25% is the sharing itself. The order-absorption vectors did not recover order specificity. THROUGHPUT CORROBORATES FILL-FLOOD A THIRD TIME: fewer/smaller tables ran faster exactly as the mechanism requires -- TN-gram -4.15% step time, capacity-control -7.20% -- but the token-law credit (-0.0025, -0.0044) is nowhere near the quality cost. BRACKETING RESULT: with E7, the n-gram capacity optimum is now bracketed on both sides. mult=5 costs +0.0079, mult=64 is the optimum, mult=256 costs +0.0109. The default was already at the knee, and this closes n-gram capacity as a direction.", "tags": ["e8", "tngram", "cp_sharing", "rejected", "capacity_knee", "duty_cycle_screen"]}
{"campaign_batch_id": "cmp_block31_e9_pm_test", "disposition": "quarantined", "entry_count": 8, "evidence_ids": [], "experiment_ids": [], "fingerprint": "7b5f499ca10cf315", "first_exp_num": 632, "last_exp_num": 639, "phase": "block31", "provenance": {"artifact_completeness": "partial", "gate_binding": false, "launch_method": "direct_ssh", "limitations": ["Runs bypassed authorize-run and have no immutable gated-experiment binding.", "mult=128 is not an adoption candidate; E7/E8 bracket the quality optimum at mult=64. Mechanism test only."], "run_records_complete": false}, "recorded_at": "2026-07-31T08:25:00Z", "recorded_by": "block31", "run_ids": [], "source_path": "campaign_log.jsonl", "source_sha256": "b22035e961d32ab9061a93d2e526cb9c90cf9d70b6c042ebcbd0d4366bb66ab7", "summary": "E9: sparse-vs-dense at NGRAM_TABLE_MULT=128, 4 pairs, 8/8 arms clean on the duty-cycle screen. A TEST OF AN ALREADY-PUBLISHED CLAIM. Paper 028 fitted penalty(m) = O - F*(m/64) on TWO points and explicitly labelled it an interpolation, not evidence, registering +14.9 ms at m=128 as the prediction awaiting a third point. MEASURED: +15.8 ms (161.6 -> 177.4 ms median step). The flat-in-m bandwidth alternative predicts +19.4 ms and is 4x further from the observation. Three-point refit: F=4.53 ms, O=24.30 ms, R^2=0.9950, break-even m=343 versus the 342 published from two points -- the parameters move by under 2%. Paper 028 stands as written. THIS ALSO CLOSES THE DIRECTION WITH A BOUND RATHER THAN A GUESS: at the quality optimum m=64 the ENTIRE fill cost is 4.53 ms of a 149.4 ms step (3.0%), so even a hypothetical zero-overhead removal of the dense embedding backward yields only -0.0018 val_bpb = 0.7 gates. No implementation of this mechanism, however perfect, can reach the adoption gate at the operating point the frame requires.", "tags": ["e9", "fill_flood", "prediction_confirmed", "out_of_sample", "direction_closed_with_bound"]}
{"campaign_batch_id": "cmp_block32_e10_depth", "disposition": "quarantined", "entry_count": 16, "evidence_ids": [], "experiment_ids": [], "fingerprint": "50cae3d55c9250fd", "first_exp_num": 640, "last_exp_num": 655, "phase": "block32", "provenance": {"artifact_completeness": "partial", "gate_binding": false, "launch_method": "direct_ssh", "limitations": ["Runs bypassed authorize-run and have no immutable gated-experiment binding.", "n=4 paired seeds only. The frame requires min_seeds=10 and NO adoption claim is made here; E11 extends depth 6 vs depth 8 to n=10. E2 is the standing precedent: it read -0.000772 at n=4 with t=-1.96, was described in situ as the campaign's best signal, and collapsed to null by n=9.", "Depths above 8 were not run: they raise IndexError on the hardcoded per-layer hash-prime families (4 bigram / 3 trigram tuples). The sweep is therefore one-sided about the optimum."], "run_records_complete": false}, "recorded_at": "2026-07-31T09:15:00Z", "recorded_by": "block32", "run_ids": [], "source_path": "campaign_log.jsonl", "source_sha256": "1b841277842631630c91d6e84ac55eee5532a5ea13ee119f0462c1991cd0421b", "summary": "E10 compute-optimal SHAPE sweep, depth {5,6,7,8} x 4 seeds at fixed 300s, width following depth through ASPECT_RATIO. All 16 arms clean on the duty-cycle screen. PAIRED vs depth 8: d7 -0.001132 (0.43 gates, 3/4); d6 -0.003252 (1.24 gates, 4/4, t=-4.70); d5 +0.045880 (17.6 gates WORSE, 0/4). This is the campaign's first lever to exceed the gate, and its first lever with a 1e-2 INTRINSIC term: the token-law decomposition of d6 vs d8 is a -0.029175 credit from +62.6% more steps against a +0.025924 intrinsic COST of removing two layers. The shallower model is much worse per token -- roughly 10 gates worse -- and wins only because throughput overpays. Every prior lever had at most one large side, which is why sixteen of them could not reach the gate. REINTERPRETATION OF THE DEPTH FLOOR, from the epoch field rather than from theory: depth 5 is the ONLY arm reaching epoch index 2, i.e. a third pass over the frozen corpus, and its 0.9784 sits beside the recorded epoch-3 collapse (exp347, 0.987). Depth 5 therefore does not fail by losing capacity; it fails by crossing the DATA WALL. Depth 6 sits just under it at 484M tokens. PREDICTION REGISTERED: stacking any further THROUGHPUT lever on top of depth 6 should NOT pay, because the marginal tokens land in epoch 3. The productive follow-up is quality-per-token.", "tags": ["e10", "depth", "compute_optimal_shape", "gate_cleared_n4", "data_wall", "pending_n10"]}
{"campaign_batch_id": "cmp_block33_e11_depth_n10", "disposition": "quarantined", "entry_count": 12, "evidence_ids": [], "experiment_ids": [], "fingerprint": "3d59a7de5ac2514e", "first_exp_num": 656, "last_exp_num": 667, "phase": "block33", "provenance": {"artifact_completeness": "partial", "gate_binding": false, "launch_method": "direct_ssh", "limitations": ["Runs bypassed authorize-run and have no immutable gated-experiment binding.", "Four of six pairs lost to a heavy co-tenant burst; only 6 clean pairs exist campaign-wide for depth 6 vs depth 8 against a frame minimum of 10. NO ADOPTION CLAIM.", "One quarantine (s51) exposed a defect in the screen that had been adopted two blocks earlier; see summary."], "run_records_complete": false}, "recorded_at": "2026-07-31T10:05:00Z", "recorded_by": "block33", "run_ids": [], "source_path": "campaign_log.jsonl", "source_sha256": "ee85bdfe97fd542d6cad82ac1c483c3f0584d87d6b03b34189a0687680286293", "summary": "E11 extended depth 6 vs depth 8 toward the frame-required n=10 and instead exposed a SCREEN DEFECT that had been introduced two blocks earlier. THE DEFECT: the duty-cycle screen, duty = steps / (BUDGET / median_step_ms), is SCALE-INVARIANT. Contention that slows every step uniformly leaves duty near 1.0 while the arm sees far fewer tokens, because duty compares an arm against its own step time. Seed 51 had duty 1.025 and 1.007, PASSED, and had a median step of 192.4 ms against a cell median of 91.8 (2.11x), completing 1598 steps against a normal ~3270. It scored 0.973186. ITS EFFECT ON THE VERDICT: under the defective duty-only screen the paired result reads n=7, mean +0.000529, 0.20 gates, 'does not clear'. Under the corrected two-sided screen it reads n=6, mean -0.002700, sd 0.001416, t=-4.67, 6/6 negative, 1.03 gates. A single arm the screen could not see moved the mean by 0.0032, larger than the effect itself. SCREEN v3, now two-sided: clean iff duty >= 0.95 AND median step time <= 1.15x the cell median. Duty catches wall clock lost OUTSIDE the steps; the band catches the steps themselves being uniformly slowed; neither sees the other failure. STATUS: depth 6 stands at 6 clean pairs, mean -0.002700 (1.03 gates), 6/6 negative. This is consistent with the n=4 reading of -0.003252 but is NOT adoptable at n=6. E12 re-runs the four lost seeds, 3-wide on the genuinely idle GPUs rather than 5-wide across busy ones.", "tags": ["e11", "depth", "screen_defect", "screen_v3", "pending_n10", "no_adoption"]}
