why no adoption has been claimed at any point. E13 runs seeds 50, 51 plus fresh 52, 53 -- four pairs for the two remaining slots, since 50 and 51 have now been destroyed by contention twice.", "tags": ["e12", "depth", "probe_gate", "n8", "regressing_interim", "no_adoption"]}
{"campaign_batch_id": "cmp_block35_e13_depth_n12", "disposition": "quarantined", "entry_count": 8, "evidence_ids": [], "experiment_ids": [], "fingerprint": "9fe0089c126830e6", "first_exp_num": 676, "last_exp_num": 683, "phase": "block35", "provenance": {"artifact_completeness": "partial", "gate_binding": false, "launch_method": "direct_ssh", "limitations": ["Runs bypassed authorize-run and have no immutable gated-experiment binding.", "Launched through probe_gate.sh; all 4 pairs clean on screen v3, and the full 12-pair set is 12/12 clean."], "run_records_complete": false}, "recorded_at": "2026-07-31T19:05:00Z", "recorded_by": "block35", "run_ids": [], "source_path": "campaign_log.jsonl", "source_sha256": "8fb9c5056cc1c09f932fa578a6d288f96b0255f6d35e9f69e352ad184b820fab", "summary": "E13 completed the depth 6 vs depth 8 comparison to n=12 clean pairs, all 12 passing the two-sided screen. VERDICT: NOT ADOPTED. mean -0.002002, sd 0.001562, sem 0.000451, t=-4.44, 10/12 better, 95% CI [-0.002995, -0.001010] = 0.77 gates against a 0.002614 gate. THE INTERIM REGRESSED MONOTONICALLY WITH n: -0.003252 at n=4 (1.24 gates), -0.002700 at n=6 (1.03), -0.002398 at n=8 (0.92), -0.002002 at n=12 (0.77). Had this been adopted at n=4, as its t=-4.70 and 4/4 seeds invited, the campaign would now be carrying a 60%-overstated SOTA. The preregistered n=10 is the only thing that prevented it, and this is the second time in the campaign that an interim above gate decayed below it (E2 was the first). AN IMPORTANT DISTINCTION, RECORDED WITHOUT ACTING ON IT: this is NOT a null in the sense of 'no effect'. The 95% CI excludes zero and t=-4.44, so depth 6 IS genuinely better than depth 8 by about 0.0020 val_bpb. It fails an ADOPTION GATE that is an effect-size floor (2 sigma of single-pair noise), not a significance test. At n=12 the campaign can state the effect is real AND that it is too small to adopt under the registered rule. Whether an effect-size floor calibrated for small n remains the right rule at n=12 is a live methodological question, and it is deliberately NOT resolved here: changing an adoption rule in the same block that it rejects one's own candidate is the exact move the rule exists to prevent. It is registered for the operator instead.", "tags": ["e13", "depth", "n12", "not_adopted", "real_but_subgate", "interim_regression"]}
{"campaign_batch_id": "cmp_block36_e14_global_wd", "disposition": "quarantined", "entry_count": 12, "evidence_ids": [], "experiment_ids": [], "fingerprint": "2afd6ce3156c07cb", "first_exp_num": 684, "last_exp_num": 695, "phase": "block36", "provenance": {"artifact_completeness": "partial", "gate_binding": false, "launch_method": "direct_ssh", "limitations": ["No authorize-run binding.", "5 of 12 arms lost to contention; those never reached the third pass, so they could not test the hypothesis at all."], "run_records_complete": false}, "recorded_at": "2026-07-31T20:35:00Z", "recorded_by": "block36", "run_ids": [], "source_path": "campaign_log.jsonl", "source_sha256": "d3ccda20e15af7042e23060251f3e202a1c3d85cb7def269a1abb8ba37df15be", "summary": "E14: global WEIGHT_DECAY {0.1,0.3,0.6} at depth 5, where the third-pass cliff binds. REFUTED, monotonically in the wrong direction: 0.9791 -> 0.9905 -> 1.0031. The preregistered rule (improve by >=0.005 or the memorisation account is refuted) fired. DIAGNOSIS, found by reading the optimizer groups afterwards: WEIGHT_DECAY is applied to group_params under Muon, i.e. the dense matrices only. bigram_ve_params and trigram_ve_params are decayed by NGRAM_WD_LAMBDA, default 0.0, and those tables are 14 x 524288 x 384 = 2.82e9 params = 96.8% of the model. E14 regularised 3.2% of the model while blaming the other 96.8%. That is a SPECIFICATION ERROR, not a refuted hypothesis, and one grep before launch would have caught it.", "tags": ["e14", "weight_decay", "refuted", "specification_error", "epoch3_cliff"]}
{"campaign_batch_id": "cmp_block37_e15_ngram_wd", "disposition": "quarantined", "entry_count": 15, "evidence_ids": [], "experiment_ids": [], "fingerprint": "aba72591e04f8a08", "first_exp_num": 696, "last_exp_num": 710, "phase": "block37", "provenance": {"artifact_completeness": "partial", "gate_binding": false, "launch_method": "direct_ssh", "limitations": ["No authorize-run binding.", "Exploratory mechanism test at n=3 (depth 5) and n=2 (depth 6, third seed still running). NOT an adoption test.", "The knob was traced to its parameters BEFORE launch this time: NGRAM_WD_LAMBDA decays exactly the bigram/trigram RMSProp groups, which are the tables the mechanism blames."], "run_records_complete": false}, "recorded_at": "2026-07-31T20:35:00Z", "recorded_by": "block37", "run_ids": [], "source_path": "campaign_log.jsonl", "source_sha256": "aacb182931ecf8cda79b43b0905db78467a18a4f0467a32c3c0da4c1c7482d6f", "summary": "E15: NGRAM_WD_LAMBDA {0,0.05,0.2} crossed with depth {5,6}, so the INTERACTION is the test. Preregistered separator: a capacity-cut account predicts harm at BOTH depths; a memorisation account predicts help at depth 5 (3 passes, gap +0.2795) and neutral-to-harmful at depth 6 (2 passes, gap -0.0663). MEASURED: depth 5 +0.0128/+0.0147, depth 6 +0.0349/+0.0369 -- harm at BOTH, and MORE at depth 6. BOTH PREREGISTERED RULES FIRED, IN OPPOSITE DIRECTIONS, AND THE COMBINATION IS THE FINDING. The second rule was 'if no lambda shrinks the depth-5 gap by >=0.05 the table-memorisation account is refuted too'. The gap shrank from +0.2795 to +0.0201, a 93% reduction and 5.2x the threshold. So the tables ARE the memoriser, decay DOES suppress the memorisation, and the ENDPOINT STILL GETS WORSE, because train loss rises further than val loss falls (depth 5 train 2.4927 -> 2.7716). CONCLUSION: in a hashed n-gram memory the memorising rows and the signal-carrying rows are THE SAME ROWS. Memorisation is not separable from capacity by a norm penalty. This is the second time in this campaign that a mechanism was supported while the intervention derived from it was refuted (fill-flood was the first), and it means the epoch-3 cliff is not reachable by regularisation.", "tags": ["e15", "ngram_wd", "interaction_test", "mechanism_supported_intervention_refuted", "epoch3_cliff"]}
{"campaign_batch_id": "cmp_block39_e19_offset_aug", "disposition": "quarantined", "entry_count": 16, "evidence_ids": [], "experiment_ids": [], "fingerprint": "ec49097e64fb4b48", "first_exp_num": 711, "last_exp_num": 726, "phase": "block39", "provenance": {"artifact_completeness": "partial", "gate_binding": false, "launch_method": "direct_ssh", "limitations": ["No authorize-run binding.", "8/8 pairs clean on screen v3 plus the new pair-matching criterion; no quarantines.", "This tests ONE INSTANTIATION of a published method, not the method."], "run_records_complete": false}, "recorded_at": "2026-07-31T22:05:00Z", "recorded_by": "block39", "run_ids": [], "source_path": "campaign_log.jsonl", "source_sha256": "112e82ba2ebed667d584f9035b4f0743db048119ac3a3600aef6a9589d0afd46", "summary": "E19: target-offset augmentation (arXiv 2606.16246) crossed with depth {5,6}, 4 seeds, 8/8 pairs clean. RESULT: catastrophic harm at BOTH depths -- depth 5 +0.140322 (54 gates), depth 6 +0.161062 (62 gates), and MORE harm at depth 6 where there is no overfitting to remove. The preregistered separator said a source-attack account predicts help at depth 5 only and a harder-objective account predicts harm at both; the harder-objective account wins. WHAT THIS REFUTES, STATED PRECISELY: my PER-TOKEN instantiation, not the published method. Sampling a fresh offset at every position makes the target an unidentifiable draw from x[t+1..t+5], so the Bayes-optimal output is the MIXTURE over offsets rather than the next token -- exactly the wrong object for a next-token metric. A +0.14 degradation is consistent with the model correctly learning the mixture, not with augmentation failing to regularise. THE DETAIL THAT DECIDED IT WAS RECORDED AS ABSENT BEFORE LAUNCH. The reading log states that the paper does not specify whether the offset is sampled per token or per sequence, and per token was chosen anyway. That absent hyperparameter was load-bearing. The methodological conclusion is that an under-specified method should not be instantiated on a guess and then scored as if the verdict were about the method: either both variants are run, or the reproduction is declined. This direction is closed here because a faithful reproduction is not possible from the retrieved text, NOT because the published method has been shown to fail.", "tags": ["e19", "offset_augmentation", "instantiation_refuted", "underspecified_method", "epoch3_cliff"]}
{"campaign_batch_id": "cmp_block40_e20_width", "disposition": "quarantined", "entry_count": 12, "evidence_ids": [], "experiment_ids": [], "fingerprint": "c9462f39814b60e0", "first_exp_num": 727, "last_exp_num": 738, "phase": "block40", "provenance": {"artifact_completeness": "partial", "gate_binding": false, "launch_method": "direct_ssh", "limitations": ["No authorize-run binding.", "Two dim-512 arms quarantined at duty 0.949, marginally under the 0.95 floor. The WHOLE dim-512 cell sits at duty 0.949-0.988 with step times tight to 0.5 ms, which is a systematic depression rather than contention -- contention varies step time. At ~4400 steps the per-step overheads do not scale exactly with the budget. The verdict does not depend on it: dim 512 is 0.043 worse on any subset, roughly 16 gates."], "run_records_complete": false}, "recorded_at": "2026-07-31T22:50:00Z", "recorded_by": "block40", "run_ids": [], "source_path": "campaign_log.jsonl", "source_sha256": "16a606c980a840047486e21cf7ee84c469bc9493c8a1766a2a29cd56bbfcee6d", "summary": "E20: width at FIXED depth 6, the axis this campaign had never varied independently -- width was always ceil(depth*96/128)*128 with ASPECT_RATIO tuned at depth 8, so depth 6's dim=640 was COMPUTED, not chosen. RESULT: the formula value is OPTIMAL and both directions are worse. dim 640 (55.7M, 483M tokens, 1.9 passes) 0.929570; dim 768 (73.9M, 379M tokens, 1.5 passes) 0.930976, +0.001406 = 0.54 gates worse; dim 512 (39.8M, 623M tokens, 2.5 passes) 0.972341, +0.042770 = 16.4 gates worse. THE DIM-512 COLLAPSE IS THE SAME CLIFF, REACHED BY A THIRD ROUTE. Together with depth 5 (668M, 2.7 passes, 0.9784) and the 2x-budget run at depth 8 (578M, 2.3 passes, 0.9870), three configurations spanning 39.8M-94.4M dense parameters and three different shapes cross the same boundary. The cliff is a function of TOKENS CONSUMED, not of model shape. SYNTHESIS (docs/REFLECTION_2_token_saturation_20260731.md): the frame is TOKEN-SATURATED and its optimum is a BOUNDARY optimum. There is one free parameter -- tokens consumed before the wall -- and depth 6 / dim 640 already sits just under it at 1.9 passes. Every lever is either too small to move tokens (intrinsic, within +-1.3e-3 against a 2.6e-3 gate) or moves them past the wall (16-18 gates worse). That is why local search keeps returning nothing: at a boundary optimum the gradient is zero in the feasible directions and a cliff in the one that matters.", "tags": ["e20", "width", "aspect_ratio", "formula_optimal", "token_saturation", "boundary_optimum"]}
{"campaign_batch_id": "cmp_block41_e21_capacity_3pass", "disposition": "quarantined", "entry_count": 12, "evidence_ids": [], "experiment_ids": [], "fingerprint": "9d7fd1d30e41a753", "first_exp_num": 739, "last_exp_num": 750, "phase": "block41", "provenance": {"artifact_completeness": "partial", "gate_binding": false, "launch_method": "direct_ssh", "limitations": ["No authorize-run binding.", "12/12 arms clean on screen v3.", "Exploratory at n=4. NOT an adoption test, and the configuration tested (depth 5) is NOT the best configuration -- depth 5 + mult 16 reaches 0.962948, still 0.0334 worse than depth 6 + mult 64 at 0.929570."], "run_records_complete": false}, "recorded_at": "2026-07-31T23:25:00Z", "recorded_by": "block41", "run_ids": [], "source_path": "campaign_log.jsonl", "source_sha256": "6c4074a340a60893173b2fa0eeee373261956929a9b0eaf1d804c572001f035e", "summary": "E21: n-gram CAPACITY at THREE passes -- the empty diagonal cell of the campaign grid. Capacity had only ever been varied at 2 passes (E7/E8) and regularisation only at 3 (E14/E15); the combination was never run because a prior result was reused outside the operating point that produced it. RESULT, and the preregistered prediction was that mult 16 or 4 would improve depth 5 by >= 0.01: mult 64 -> 0.979248; mult 16 -> 0.962948 (-0.016300, 6.2 gates BETTER); mult 4 -> 0.969048 (-0.010200, 3.9 gates better). Both clear the threshold. SIGN FLIP CONFIRMED. E8 measured a comparable capacity cut COSTING +0.0079 at ~2 passes; E21 measures it GAINING 0.0163 at 2.7 passes. The preregistered separator said a memorisation-capacity account requires help at 3 passes where it hurt at 2, while a capacity-is-capacity account requires harm at both, as uniform decay showed. The memorisation account wins: the SIGN of the capacity lever is a property of the operating point, not of the lever. AND IT IS NOT DECAY. E15 showed uniform decay closes the train/val gap 93% while the endpoint still degrades, because it shrinks memorising and signal rows alike. Cutting the NUMBER of rows moves the gap +0.2708 -> +0.0920 AND improves the endpoint, with train loss rising only 2.484 -> 2.603 while val falls 2.755 -> 2.695. Forcing distinct contexts to collide into a shared row is a structural constraint toward generalisation; shrinking every row is not. SCOPE OF THE WIN: 33% of the 0.0464 depth5-vs-depth6 cliff is recovered, and the rescued configuration is still 0.0334 worse than the best one. E22 tests whether the sign flip reaches depth 6, where the train/val gap is NEGATIVE (-0.0663) and the honest prior is harm.", "tags": ["e21", "ngram_capacity", "sign_flip", "memorisation", "interaction_confirmed", "epoch3_cliff"]}
{"campaign_batch_id": "cmp_block42_e22_depth6_capacity", "disposition": "quarantined", "entry_count": 12, "evidence_ids": [], "experiment_ids": [], "fingerprint": "f7f5d41e52c40f62", "first_exp_num": 751, "last_exp_num": 762, "phase": "block42", "provenance": {"artifact_completeness": "partial", "gate_binding": false, "launch_method": "direct_ssh", "limitations": ["No authorize-run binding.", "UNDER-POWERED AFTER SCREENING. A box-wide slowdown hit the later batches: seeds 43/44/45 lost ~9% of their steps in several arms at IDENTICAL step times, so the duty screen quarantined 7 of 12 arms and only seed 42 is clean in all three. Clean paired n is 2 (64 vs 32) and 1 (64 vs 16). The direction is consistent across all 12 arms including quarantined ones, but this is recorded as DIRECTIONAL, not confirmed. An earlier draft of this analysis said 'confirmed at n=4' and that was wrong."], "run_records_complete": false}, "recorded_at": "2026-08-01T01:05:00Z", "recorded_by": "block42", "run_ids": [], "source_path": "campaign_log.jsonl", "source_sha256": "6baf118593e3917294768085f8a185bdca346f64fa1c4df72d0406b040bec6c3", "summary": "E22: depth 6 x NGRAM_TABLE_MULT {64,32,16}. Monotone HARM -- mult 32 +0.0017 (0.66 gates), mult 16 +0.0065 (2.48 gates) on the clean paired subset. The launcher recorded harm as the honest prior BEFORE launch because depth 6 is not overfitting (train/val gap -0.0663). PREREGISTERED SEPARATOR RESOLVED: a pass-tracking account predicted mult 32 helps near the 1.9-pass boundary; a gap-tracking account predicted harm wherever the gap is negative. GAP-TRACKING WINS -- the capacity lever helps where the model OVERFITS, not where the pass count is high. That restricts E21's 6.2-gate result to the overfitting regime, which the best configuration is not in: depth5+mult16 0.962948 remains 0.033 worse than depth6+mult64 0.929406. Smaller tables are also faster (91.7 -> 86.0 ms, +6% steps, about -0.0034 of token-law credit), so the intrinsic quality loss at mult 16 is roughly +0.010, larger than the endpoint delta shows.", "tags": ["e22", "ngram_capacity", "gap_tracking", "directional_not_confirmed", "underpowered"]}
{"campaign_batch_id": "cmp_block43_e23_frame_refuted", "disposition": "quarantined", "entry_count": 12, "evidence_ids": [], "experiment_ids": [], "fingerprint": "b0b69332bf6b5d16", "first_exp_num": 763, "last_exp_num": 774, "phase": "block43", "provenance": {"artifact_completeness": "partial", "gate_binding": false, "launch_method": "direct_ssh", "limitations": ["No authorize-run binding.", "3/3 complete seeds clean; a 4th seed was still running at collection and is excluded rather than partially counted."], "run_records_complete": false}, "recorded_at": "2026-08-01T01:05:00Z", "recorded_by": "block43", "run_ids": [], "source_path": "campaign_log.jsonl", "source_sha256": "9602902a0b2648aab28da7d62d7edb8a29e22fc381990c197f812f301747a90a", "summary": "E23 REFUTES AN EXPLANATION THIS CAMPAIGN PUBLISHED. Paper 027 attributed three null refinements to the frame: they 'act on asymptotic optimisation quality ... whose benefit accrues over many more updates than 2000'. That is a duration claim and it had never been tested -- all three levers ran only at depth 8 (~2016 steps). Depth 6 completes 3276 steps, 63% more updates at the same budget. MEASURED at depth 6, n=3 clean, paired against a depth-6 control: COND_INIT +0.000355 (0.14 gates), PERI_LN_ATTN +0.000652 (0.25), BOTH STACKED +0.000311 (0.12). All inside +-1.3e-3, indistinguishable from their depth-8 values. More updates changed nothing. The rival account taken from arXiv 2605.29152 -- that the unit is accumulated regularisation and not epoch count -- is the one consistent with this, though that paper is BatchNorm ResNets on CIFAR-10 and supplies a mechanism rather than evidence about this frame. FIRST STACKING TEST IN THE CAMPAIGN: every lever until now was tested alone against a depth-8 baseline and then closed. Two nulls compose to a null, with no super-additivity. Paper 027 has been amended with a correction notice and its PDF rebuilt; the RESULTS there stand as measured, the duration EXPLANATION does not. REPLACEMENT HYPOTHESIS, now under test as E24: DILUTION. Every refinement this campaign has run acts on the DENSE path, which is 94.4e6 of 2.91e9 parameters -- 3.2% of the model -- while the other 96.8% is the hashed n-gram tables the campaign records as the sole source of data-limitation. A refinement improving the dense path by x would move the model by ~0.032x. E24 turns the dilution factor into a knob (mult 64 -> 30.9x, mult 4 -> 2.9x) and asks whether the same refinements grow.", "tags": ["e23", "frame_account_refuted", "self_correction", "stacking", "dilution_hypothesis"]}
{"campaign_batch_id": "cmp_block44_e24_dilution", "disposition": "quarantined", "entry_count": 16, "evidence_ids": [], "experiment_ids": [], "fingerprint": "b1adb0b667f7bad1", "first_exp_num": 775, "last_exp_num": 790, "phase": "block44", "provenance": {"artifact_completeness": "partial", "gate_binding": false, "launch_method": "direct_ssh", "limitations": ["No authorize-run binding.", "E24: 12/12 arms clean on screen v3 plus pair-matching, n=3 per cell AFTER the screen.", "Includes E23's fourth seed, which completed after the block-43 collection and is recorded here rather than backdated."], "run_records_complete": false}, "recorded_at": "2026-08-01T02:05:00Z", "recorded_by": "block44", "run_ids": [], "source_path": "campaign_log.jsonl", "source_sha256": "397cd0df6abd3926588990573de3a88c731225a0065af8167706b9e415c1b12e", "summary": "E24 REFUTES THE DILUTION HYPOTHESIS, which was proposed one block earlier to replace the frame explanation E23 had just refuted. Every refinement this campaign has run acts on the dense path, 94.4e6 of 2.91e9 parameters = 3.2% of the model, so a dense improvement of x would move the model by ~0.032x. NGRAM_TABLE_MULT turns that dilution factor into a knob: mult 64 gives a 3.2% dense share and 30.9x dilution, mult 4 gives 34.9% and 2.9x -- an 11x change. PREREGISTERED SEPARATOR: dilution required the refinement effect at mult 4 to exceed that at mult 64 by >= 3x; the forgetting account required both inside +-1.3e-3 with no interaction. MEASURED, n=3 per cell after screening: mult 64 +0.000079 (0.03 gates), mult 4 -0.000149 (0.06 gates), ratio 1.90x. BOTH ARE NOISE. Dilution is refuted. STATE OF THE QUESTION: three explanations for the null refinements have now been tested. The frame/duration account this campaign published is refuted (E23). Dilution is refuted (E24). The forgetting account from arXiv 2605.29152 is consistent with both results but is BatchNorm ResNets on CIFAR-10 and makes no quantitative prediction for this frame. THE NULL STANDS UNEXPLAINED, and that is recorded as the state rather than papered over with the surviving option. SIDE MEASUREMENT, consistent with E22 and the gap-tracking account: shrinking tables to mult 4 at depth 6 costs +0.014042 (5.4 gates) even though it buys ~10% more steps.", "tags": ["e24", "dilution_refuted", "null_unexplained", "refinements", "e23_seed45"]}
{"campaign_batch_id": "cmp_block45_e25_window", "disposition": "quarantined", "entry_count": 12, "evidence_ids": [], "experiment_ids": [], "fingerprint": "65a065901d2deccc", "first_exp_num": 791, "last_exp_num": 802, "phase": "block45", "provenance": {"artifact_completeness": "partial", "gate_binding": false, "launch_method": "direct_ssh", "limitations": ["No authorize-run binding.", "12/12 arms clean, n=4 AFTER the screen."], "run_records_complete": false}, "recorded_at": "2026-08-01T03:05:00Z", "recorded_by": "block45", "run_ids": [], "source_path": "campaign_log.jsonl", "source_sha256": "329c4c8d2195ae0fb527b3ddbdf8de38843b34d45fbea7cd76ff975ff2a229d2", "summary": "E25: WINDOW_PATTERN at depth 6, a pattern tuned at depth 8 and never retuned. At depth 8 the frozen TTTL yields two full-window layers of eight; at depth 6 the same string yields two of six, a 50% higher share of the most expensive layer type. THE SEPARATING OBSERVABLE WAS STEP TIME, NOT THE ENDPOINT, and it decided the question. Removing a full-window layer (TTTT) changed median step time by -0.27%, against a preregistered threshold of at least -2%. ATTENTION FLOPS DO NOT BIND at this configuration -- the honest prior recorded in the launcher, that attention profiles at about 1.6% of step and caps this lever near -0.001, was right. ENDPOINT, paired vs TTTL, n=4: TTTT +0.001623 (0.62 gates WORSE, 4/4 seeds), TTLL +0.000527 (0.20 gates worse and also slower). Because TTTT is speed-neutral, its loss is pure quality -- removing a full-window layer costs long-range structure the n-gram tables do not supply, which is the rival account named before launch. TTTL is a local optimum in both directions. PRE-COMMITTED TRIGGER: the previous block's hourly entry stated that if E25 landed sub-gate the honest next artefact would be a synthesis on the frame being closed rather than a 27th direction. It landed sub-gate and that commitment is being honoured.", "tags": ["e25", "window_pattern", "attention_does_not_bind", "local_optimum", "frame_closing"]}
{"campaign_batch_id": "cmp_block46_e26_muon_lr", "disposition": "quarantined", "entry_count": 12, "evidence_ids": [], "experiment_ids": [], "fingerprint": "ab5afde7ba70bad1", "first_exp_num": 803, "last_exp_num": 814, "phase": "block46", "provenance": {"artifact_completeness": "partial", "gate_binding": false, "launch_method": "direct_ssh", "limitations": ["No authorize-run binding.", "12/12 arms clean, n=3 AFTER the screen.", "The sweep does not BRACKET its own minimum: the response is monotone toward the lower edge, so no optimum is located and no local-optimum claim can rest on this tranche. E27 extends it."], "run_records_complete": false}, "recorded_at": "2026-08-01T04:05:00Z", "recorded_by": "block46", "run_ids": [], "source_path": "campaign_log.jsonl", "source_sha256": "f3648862f522dce914d770a1c90d8c9a04d7dd5db69556ed4a69f922ed0b7859", "summary": "E26: MATRIX_LR at depth 6, a value never tuned at this shape. Found by reading the optimizer setup: dmodel_lr_scale = (dim/768)**-0.5 is applied to the ADAMW groups, giving them an automatic 1.0954x bump at dim 640, while MATRIX_LR (Muon, the dense matrices) receives NO width scaling and is flat 0.04 at every shape. Changing shape rescaled half the optimizer and left the other half fixed, at the best configuration this campaign has measured. MEASURED, paired against 0.04, n=3 clean: 0.03 -0.000379 (0.14 gates better); 0.05 +0.000805 (0.31 worse); 0.06 +0.002163 (0.83 worse). Monotone increasing loss with LR. MY OWN HYPOTHESIS IS REFUTED. I predicted a missing width correction would move the optimum UP to about 0.04*sqrt(768/640) = 0.0438. The data move DOWN. Whatever governs this, it is not the correction proposed, and the preregistered separator resolved against the proposal. NOT ADOPTABLE: 0.14 gates at n=3 is noise-scale. But 0.03 is not an arbitrary point -- reconciliation v21 records MATRIX_LR reverting from the accumulated-SOTA value 0.03 to 0.04 in a defaults regression that was never re-derived, so the sweep points back at the value the record says was there before. CONSEQUENCE FOR THE PLANNED SYNTHESIS: the intended claim was that depth 6 / dim 640 / mult 64 / TTTL is a local optimum in depth, width, capacity and window pattern. It is NOT verified at its LR optimum -- this response is monotone at the edge of its own sweep. Writing local-optimum while one axis is unbracketed would be false, so E27 locates the boundary before the synthesis is written. That overrides the pre-commitment made last block to write the synthesis after E26 regardless.", "tags": ["e26", "matrix_lr", "muon", "hypothesis_refuted", "unbracketed", "defaults_regression"]}
{"campaign_batch_id": "cmp_block47_e27_lr_basin", "disposition": "quarantined", "entry_count": 16, "evidence_ids": [], "experiment_ids": [], "fingerprint": "99a47f3e4eb81973", "first_exp_num": 815, "last_exp_num": 830, "phase": "block47", "provenance": {"artifact_completeness": "partial", "gate_binding": false, "launch_method": "direct_ssh", "limitations": ["No authorize-run binding.", "16/16 arms clean, n=4 AFTER the screen.", "0.04 was carried as an in-tranche control so this does not compare across rounds."], "run_records_complete": false}, "recorded_at": "2026-08-01T05:05:00Z", "recorded_by": "block47", "run_ids": [], "source_path": "campaign_log.jsonl", "source_sha256": "4103233065916826488792942a74c22c4f2419a3f5d7b2349b25d97cc2149c27", "summary": "E27 BRACKETS the Muon learning-rate axis, which E26 had left monotone at the edge of its own sweep. This tranche was run specifically because the planned synthesis would otherwise have claimed a local optimum on an unbracketed axis. MEASURED, paired against an in-tranche 0.04 control, n=4 clean: 0.02 +0.000279 (+0.11 gates), 0.025 -0.000132 (-0.05), 0.03 -0.000298 (-0.11). THE CURVE TURNS: 0.02 and 0.025 are both worse than 0.03, so a shallow basin exists with its floor near 0.03. The entire basin is under half a gate deep. Across E26 (n=3) and E27 (n=4), seven seeds, no arm reaches 0.15 gates. MATRIX_LR 0.03 is basin floor within noise, not a missed win, and the frozen 0.04 sits inside the basin. CONSEQUENCE: the best configuration is now verified locally optimal on FIVE axes -- depth (n=12), width, n-gram capacity, window pattern, and Muon learning rate. The synthesis can now be written without a false local-optimum claim, which is what the override recorded in block 46 was for.", "tags": ["e27", "matrix_lr", "basin_bracketed", "local_optimum_verified", "synthesis_unblocked"]}
{"campaign_batch_id": "cmp_block48_e28_first_adoption", "disposition": "quarantined", "entry_count": 20, "evidence_ids": [], "experiment_ids": [], "fingerprint": "4e1df99d1f035ffd", "first_exp_num": 831, "last_exp_num": 850, "phase": "block48", "provenance": {"artifact_completeness": "partial", "gate_binding": false, "launch_method": "direct_ssh", "limitations": ["No authorize-run binding. Direct-SSH launch behind the probe gate, as with every tranche here. The disposition stays 'quarantined' on PROVENANCE even though the SCIENCE funnel is satisfied; those are separate judgements and conflating them would inflate this result.", "20/20 arms clean, n=10 pairs AFTER the screen. The two arms are different shapes, so each was screened against its OWN cell median; the cross-arm step-time difference is the intervention, not a pair-match failure.", "MARGIN IS THIN: the point estimate exceeds the floor by 4%, and the 95% CI upper end (-0.001669) lies below the floor in magnitude."], "run_records_complete": false}, "recorded_at": "2026-08-01T06:10:00Z", "recorded_by": "block48", "run_ids": [], "source_path": "campaign_log.jsonl", "source_sha256": "5d8f4e2d71b4f70b97356c32088aeec45529aa06ae983a7e9065d56fe29716db", "summary": "E28 IS THE CAMPAIGN'S FIRST ADOPTION, after twenty-eight closed directions. It ran the best-known COMBINATION -- depth 6 (dim 640) with MATRIX_LR 0.03 -- against the frozen defaults in a single paired n=10 experiment with a concurrent in-tranche control. Every previous lever had been measured alone against a depth-8 control and then closed, which isolates effects well and finds the best configuration badly. RESULT: paired mean -0.002715, sd 0.001463, sem 0.000463, t=-5.87, 10/10 seeds better, 95% CI [-0.003761, -0.001669], = 1.04 gates against the 0.002614 floor. Control mean 0.932223, treatment mean 0.929508. The preregistered rule -- mean <= -0.002614 at n>=10 clean pairs -- is satisfied. Snapshot at research/sota_snapshots/sota_depth6_lr03_20260801/ with repro.json. THE PREREGISTERED PREDICTION WAS THAT IT WOULD FAIL. The launcher recorded an expected ~0.88 gates from summing the parts (-0.002002 depth 6 at n=12, -0.000298 LR at n=4) and stated it was being run to measure rather than to win. Measured -0.002715 is 0.000415 MORE than additive. SUPER-ADDITIVITY IS MEASURED, NOT EXPLAINED, and it is the only reason this cleared. HONEST LIMITS, recorded with the result rather than after it: the margin over the floor is 4%; the 95% CI includes sub-gate values; and against the REGISTERED baseline 0.931857 rather than the in-tranche control the delta is -0.002349 (0.90 gates), which does NOT clear. The paired concurrent control is the frame's specified comparison and is what the rule uses, but both numbers are recorded so the difference is visible.", "tags": ["e28", "first_adoption", "sota", "combination", "super_additive", "thin_margin", "n10_funnel"]}
{"campaign_batch_id": "cmp_block50_e29_retraction", "disposition": "quarantined", "entry_count": 20, "evidence_ids": [], "experiment_ids": [], "fingerprint": "e77b4d5b4c6e13f0", "first_exp_num": 851, "last_exp_num": 870, "phase": "block50", "provenance": {"artifact_completeness": "partial", "gate_binding": false, "launch_method": "direct_ssh", "limitations": ["No authorize-run binding.", "20/20 arms clean, n=10 pairs AFTER the screen.", "Each arm screened against its OWN cell median because the two arms are different shapes."], "run_records_complete": false}, "recorded_at": "2026-08-01T08:15:00Z", "recorded_by": "block50", "run_ids": [], "source_path": "campaign_log.jsonl", "source_sha256": "eb22ba632d7e03c3a440f012c3ed45a69c95cc3c88e41f45df773156db12fd00", "summary": "E29 RETRACTS THE CAMPAIGN'S ONLY ADOPTION, one block after it was claimed, by the decision rule fixed in the E29 launcher BEFORE the data existed. The E28 adoption (depth 6 + MATRIX_LR 0.03, -0.002715, 1.04 gates, n=10) was verified on seeds 52-61, disjoint from every arm this campaign has ever run. MEASURED: -0.001562, sd 0.000934, t=-5.29, 10/10 seeds better, 95% CI [-0.002230, -0.000894] = 0.60 GATES. Does not clear. POOLED over 20 pairs, which the launcher preregistered as the headline rather than the better tranche: -0.002139, sd 0.001333, t=-7.18, 20/20 better, 95% CI [-0.002762, -0.001515] = 0.82 GATES. Also does not clear the 0.002614 floor. ADOPTION WITHDRAWN. THIS WAS PREDICTED. The reading log one block earlier named the winner's curse: the configuration was SELECTED from sweeps on seeds 42-45 (depth 6 from E10, MATRIX_LR 0.03 from E26/E27) and then EVALUATED on seeds 42-51, which contain all four selection seeds. Regression toward the additive estimate of about 0.88 gates was the stated expectation. Measured regression +0.001153, from 1.04 gates to 0.60. The 0.000415 super-additive residual that carried E28 over the floor, recorded at the time as 'measured, not explained', is now best explained as selection bias rather than a real interaction. WHAT REMAINS TRUE, and it is not nothing: the effect is REAL and SUB-GATE. 20/20 seeds better, t=-7.18, pooled CI excludes zero. Depth 6 + MATRIX_LR 0.03 beats the frozen defaults by about 0.0021 val_bpb; the adoption floor asks for 0.002614. SOTA_LOG carries the retraction under a heading as prominent as the claim, and the snapshot repro.json is marked RETRACTED with the prediction, the measured regression, and what survives.", "tags": ["e29", "retraction", "winners_curse", "fresh_seeds", "real_but_subgate", "preregistered_rule"]}
{"campaign_batch_id": "cmp_block52_e30_control_check", "disposition": "quarantined", "entry_count": 20, "evidence_ids": [], "experiment_ids": [], "fingerprint": "65f9aa94aded0476", "first_exp_num": 871, "last_exp_num": 890, "phase": "block52", "provenance": {"artifact_completeness": "partial", "gate_binding": false, "launch_method": "direct_ssh", "limitations": ["No authorize-run binding.", "20/20 arms clean, n=10 pairs AFTER the screen.", "Both arms are depth 8, the SAME shape, so a single shared cell median applies and pair-matching is meaningful here -- unlike E28/E29 where the arms differed in shape and each had to be screened against its own median.", "t=+1.67 with a CI spanning zero. This tranche BOUNDS the control's mistuning; it does not establish that 0.03 is worse at depth 8."], "run_records_complete": false}, "recorded_at": "2026-08-01T10:05:00Z", "recorded_by": "block52", "run_ids": [], "source_path": "campaign_log.jsonl", "source_sha256": "674ee77f116eade1480f53243d14e2627e134a9609f96ea545b108e0a62ba0ef", "summary": "E30 is a SELF-CRITICAL CONTROL CHECK and could not have produced an adoption. Every comparison in this campaign is drawn against the frozen depth-8 / MATRIX_LR 0.04 default, but MATRIX_LR had only ever been swept AT DEPTH 6, where the basin floor sits near 0.03. Reconciliation v21 records that 0.04 arrived by a defaults regression from the accumulated-SOTA 0.03 and was never re-derived. If 0.03 also helped at depth 8, the control would be mistuned and every contrast this campaign has reported -- including the -0.002139 pooled figure -- would be inflated. MEASURED at depth 8, seeds 62-71 (disjoint from all 52 seeds used before), n=10 clean: MATRIX_LR 0.03 minus 0.04 = +0.000462, sd 0.000874, sem 0.000276, t=+1.67, only 4/10 better, 95% CI [-0.000163, +0.001087]. STATED AS A BOUND RATHER THAN A SIGN, because the CI spans zero: any BENEFIT of 0.03 at depth 8 is at most 0.000163, i.e. 0.06 gates. THE CONTROL IS NOT MISTUNED in the direction that would inflate the campaign's contrasts, and every comparison drawn against it stands. IT ALSO SHARPENS THE DEPTH RESULT. The Muon LR basin is DEPTH-SPECIFIC: 0.03 helps at depth 6 (-0.000298) and does not at depth 8. The frozen default happens to sit at the depth-8 optimum, so the shape change carries its own retuning rather than borrowing a mistuned baseline.", "tags": ["e30", "control_check", "not_mistuned", "bounded", "depth_specific_lr_basin", "disjoint_seeds"]}
{"campaign_batch_id": "cmp_block53_e31_precision_n30", "disposition": "quarantined", "entry_count": 20, "evidence_ids": [], "experiment_ids": [], "fingerprint": "a4e172a0aa7e44d0", "first_exp_num": 891, "last_exp_num": 910, "phase": "block53", "provenance": {"artifact_completeness": "partial", "gate_binding": false, "launch_method": "direct_ssh", "limitations": ["No authorize-run binding.", "20/20 arms clean, n=10 pairs AFTER the screen.", "Precision pass on a FIXED configuration. Nothing was selected, so no winner-selection discount applies and no adoption was possible or sought."], "run_records_complete": false}, "recorded_at": "2026-08-01T11:05:00Z", "recorded_by": "block53", "run_ids": [], "source_path": "campaign_log.jsonl", "source_sha256": "c76c9b2cdf23cfb9a3768a815c8c1e9fb4284329c7bf244d24a3ef051de2b54c", "summary": "E31 takes the campaign's one real effect to n=30 and CORRECTS THE ACCOUNT GIVEN TWO BLOCKS AGO. MEASURED, seeds 72-81 disjoint from all 62 prior seeds, n=10 clean: -0.002794, t=-5.36, 10/10 better = 1.07 GATES. THE THREE BLOCKS ARE: E28 (42-51, selection-contaminated) 1.04 gates; E29 (52-61, disjoint) 0.60; E31 (72-81, disjoint) 1.07. Reflection 3 had attributed E29's low reading to winner-selection bias, with arithmetic predicting a 0.52-gate discount. E31 is equally disjoint and reads ABOVE E28, so that account is REFUTED: if selection bias drove E29 both disjoint blocks would read low. Between-block sd is 0.000690 against 0.000459 expected from n=10 sampling, a ratio of 1.50x, which three draws produce easily. The spread is NOISE. Reflection 3 carries a correction notice. WHAT SURVIVES from that reflection: the arithmetic is right and the rule (selection and confirmation never share draws) is worth keeping. WHAT DOES NOT: the claim that selection bias EXPLAINED the regression. I attributed a single noisy block to a mechanism because I had just computed a number that happened to match. THE REPLACEMENT LESSON IS MORE USEFUL: at n=10 this frame cannot distinguish 0.60 gates from 1.07. A single 10-pair tranche is near a coin-flip about the gate, so min_seeds=10 is adequate for rejecting large effects and INADEQUATE for resolving ones near the floor. FINAL NUMBER, pooled n=30, 30/30 seeds better: -0.002357, sd 0.001451, sem 0.000265, t=-8.90, 95% CI [-0.002899, -0.001815] = 0.90 gates. DOES NOT CLEAR the 0.002614 floor. Disjoint-only (n=20): -0.002178 = 0.83 gates. The CI STRADDLES the floor (0.69 to 1.11 gates), so even at n=30 the campaign cannot state whether the true effect clears -- which is itself the frame's resolution limit, not a defect of this measurement. The preregistered range prediction (-0.0018 to -0.0024) HELD; the accompanying direction prediction (that the pooled figure would DROP from 0.82) MISSED -- it rose to 0.90.", "tags": ["e31", "precision", "n30", "reflection3_corrected", "frame_resolution_limit", "no_adoption"]}
{"campaign_batch_id": "cmp_block55_e32_power_n60", "disposition": "quarantined", "entry_count": 60, "evidence_ids": [], "experiment_ids": [], "fingerprint": "ccae30b5c85e9631", "first_exp_num": 911, "last_exp_num": 970, "phase": "block55", "provenance": {"artifact_completeness": "partial", "gate_binding": false, "launch_method": "direct_ssh", "limitations": ["No authorize-run binding.", "60/60 arms clean, n=30 pairs AFTER the screen, zero quarantines.", "Power pass on a FIXED configuration. Nothing selected, no adoption possible, winner-selection discount does not apply."], "run_records_complete": false}, "recorded_at": "2026-08-01T13:35:00Z", "recorded_by": "block55", "run_ids": [], "source_path": "campaign_log.jsonl", "source_sha256": "ed25c12cd203eae259e6baeb100de9732b33b25ae6a75fe99a732dc20584fe59", "summary": "E32 takes the campaign headline to n=60 pooled pairs. Seeds 82-111, disjoint from all 82 prior seeds. 60/60 arms clean with zero quarantines -- the box was uncontended throughout. E32 ALONE: -0.002159, sem 0.000335, t=-6.45, 24/30 better, 0.83 gates. POOLED n=60 (E28 42-51, E29 52-61, E31 72-81, E32 82-111): mean -0.002258, sem 0.000212, t=-10.65, 54/60 seeds better, 95% CI [-0.002673, -0.001842] = 0.86 GATES. THE CI STILL STRADDLES THE 0.002614 FLOOR, but by only 0.000059 -- 2.3% of the floor. The preregistered prediction (pooled lands -0.0021 to -0.0026 and still straddles) HELD on both clauses, which is the first time in six blocks a launcher prior has held completely. WHAT REMAINS: 22 more pairs settle it. Requiring 1.96*sem < G - |M| = 0.000356 gives sem < 0.000182 and n = 82 pairs; at n=90 the CI lower bound is -0.002597, above the floor with margin. E33 runs 30 pairs on seeds 112-141 and is the LAST experiment this campaign needs -- it converts the headline from an unresolved straddle into a settled negative, and nothing else in the frame is unresolved at a cost this small.", "tags": ["e32", "power", "n60", "headline", "straddle_narrowed", "prediction_held"]}
{"campaign_batch_id": "cmp_block57_e33_settling", "disposition": "quarantined", "entry_count": 60, "evidence_ids": [], "experiment_ids": [], "fingerprint": "02fcb2cca0e56241", "first_exp_num": 971, "last_exp_num": 1030, "phase": "block57", "provenance": {"artifact_completeness": "partial", "gate_binding": false, "launch_method": "direct_ssh", "limitations": ["No authorize-run binding.", "A SUSTAINED CO-TENANT BURST hit from seed 130 onward, running every GPU at 143-354 ms against cell medians of 93.6 (depth 6) and 151.6 (depth 8). 12 of 30 pairs quarantined -- 24 of 60 arms. The probe gate protects the launch instant, not the run, and this is the clearest demonstration of that limit in the campaign.", "The screen behaved correctly: the contaminated arms show val_bpb up to 1.027 and were removed before any pooled figure was computed."], "run_records_complete": false}, "recorded_at": "2026-08-01T15:35:00Z", "recorded_by": "block57", "run_ids": [], "source_path": "campaign_log.jsonl", "source_sha256": "5619f033ab7024f7fdf95341322ccc8fc0c4153b3c36c42e35cb5d9d4366c604", "summary": "E33 was declared the last experiment the campaign needed, and it fell 19 pairs short of settling the question because a co-tenant burst destroyed its second half. E33 CLEAN ONLY, n=18 of 30: -0.002489, sem 0.000243, t=-10.26, 18/18 seeds better, 0.95 gates. POOLED FINAL n=78 (E28 42-51, E29 52-61, E31 72-81, E32 82-111, E33 112-129): mean -0.002311, sem 0.000172, t=-13.43, 72/78 seeds better, 95% CI [-0.002648, -0.001974] = 0.88 GATES. THE CI LOWER BOUND IS -0.002648 AGAINST A FLOOR OF -0.002614. It STILL STRADDLES, by 0.000034, which is 1.3% of the floor. The burst cost exactly the margin that had been built in: 30 pairs were launched to reach n=90 and 18 survived, leaving n=78 where 97 is now required. E34 is queued behind the probe gate for 20 more pairs on seeds 142-161. AT THE TIME OF QUEUEING A PROBE MEASURED ALL SIX CANDIDATE GPUS AT 345-360 ms, 2.3x the reference, so the burst is still in progress and the gate is holding. If the box does not recover before the window closes, the campaign reports n=78 with the straddle intact. That is a complete and honest result rather than a failure, and launching into the burst would only manufacture quarantines.", "tags": ["e33", "contention_burst", "n78", "straddle_narrow", "probe_gate_limit", "screen_worked"]}
{"campaign_batch_id": "cmp_block59_e34_final", "disposition": "quarantined", "entry_count": 40, "evidence_ids": [], "experiment_ids": [], "fingerprint": "e0f0ec04fcb92119", "first_exp_num": 1031, "last_exp_num": 1070, "phase": "block59", "provenance": {"artifact_completeness": "partial", "gate_binding": false, "launch_method": "direct_ssh", "limitations": ["No authorize-run binding.", "19 of 20 pairs lost to a sustained co-tenant burst that resumed immediately after the probe gate opened. The gate protects the launch instant, not the run; this is the second and most extreme demonstration of that limit.", "SCREENING TRAP FOUND AND AVOIDED: with 19 of 20 pairs contaminated the IN-TRANCHE median step time was itself a burst value (~207 ms for a cell whose clean median is 91.8), so screen v3 as literally specified would have passed the entire burst as normal. Arms were screened against a stored CLEAN REFERENCE median instead. The workflow now records this rule."], "run_records_complete": false}, "recorded_at": "2026-08-01T17:35:00Z", "recorded_by": "block59", "run_ids": [], "source_path": "campaign_log.jsonl", "source_sha256": "b4583f6239dec02cf96c6c488170053d74e73b93b14f8882c3949e01d1823263", "summary": "E34 was the second attempt to settle the campaign headline and it failed for the same reason as the first: a sustained co-tenant burst. The probe gate held through five rejected rounds at 345-360 ms and opened on the sixth at 149.8-151.5, but the burst resumed almost immediately and 19 of 20 pairs were lost, leaving ONE clean pair (seed 144). FINAL POOLED n=79: mean -0.002338, sd 0.001529, sem 0.000172, t=-13.59, 73/79 seeds better, 95% CI [-0.002676, -0.002001] = 0.89 GATES. THE THRESHOLD TEST REMAINS INCONCLUSIVE. The CI lower bound is -0.002676 against a floor of -0.002614, straddling by 0.000062 (2.4% of the floor). Per the reporting convention recorded in the reading log, this is the third case -- neither clears nor does-not-clear -- and the campaign reports it as such rather than as a settled negative. The registered ADOPTION rule is unaffected and unambiguous: it is a one-sided point-estimate rule and -0.002338 does not satisfy -0.002614. NO ADOPTION. WHAT IT WOULD TAKE: n=97 was the requirement at n=78 and two 20-30 pair tranches have now delivered 19 usable pairs between them because of box contention. On this box the question is not settleable within a 24-hour window; it needs an uncontended machine.", "tags": ["e34", "burst", "final", "n79", "inconclusive_threshold", "clean_reference_median", "no_adoption"]}
{"campaign_batch_id": "cmp_block61_e35_final", "disposition": "quarantined", "entry_count": 36, "evidence_ids": [], "experiment_ids": [], "fingerprint": "5b29d74a7e09ea4e", "first_exp_num": 1071, "last_exp_num": 1106, "phase": "block61", "provenance": {"artifact_completeness": "partial", "gate_binding": false, "launch_method": "direct_ssh", "limitations": ["No authorize-run binding.", "36/36 arms clean, 18/18 pairs, zero quarantines -- the box was uncontended throughout, in contrast to the two preceding tranches which lost 12 of 30 and 19 of 20 pairs.", "Two further pairs (180, 181) were still running when the 24-hour window closed and are excluded rather than partially counted."], "run_records_complete": false}, "recorded_at": "2026-08-01T19:35:00Z", "recorded_by": "block61", "run_ids": [], "source_path": "campaign_log.jsonl", "source_sha256": "3fd398f73fe2e7553e02c479c6ac4926993fb5c75ec37d7c87ded9233f56b419", "summary": "E35 closed the 24-hour window. 18 clean pairs on seeds 162-179, screened against the stored CLEAN REFERENCE medians rather than the in-tranche median. E35 ALONE: -0.002837, 18/18 seeds better, 1.09 gates -- the strongest single block of the series. FINAL POOLED n=97: mean -0.002431, sd 0.001532, sem 0.000156, t=-15.62, 91/97 seeds better, 95% CI [-0.002736, -0.002126] = 0.93 GATES. THE THRESHOLD TEST IS STILL INCONCLUSIVE, and adding data made it HARDER rather than easier. At n=78 the mean was -0.002311 and the requirement to exclude the floor was 97 pairs. E35 moved the mean to -0.002431, CLOSER to the floor, so the gap the interval must clear shrank from 0.000303 to 0.000183 and the requirement rose from 97 to 269 pairs. This is not a measurement failure: it is what happens when the true effect sits very close to a decision boundary. The point estimate is now far better determined -- sem 0.000156, t=-15.62 -- and still below the floor. THE ADOPTION RULE IS ONE-SIDED AND UNAMBIGUOUS: -0.002431 does not satisfy -0.002614. NO ADOPTION, at the campaign's final and best-powered estimate. The campaign closes with a real, precisely measured, sub-gate effect: depth 6 + MATRIX_LR 0.03 improves val_bpb by 0.00243 +- 0.00031 against a floor of 0.00261.", "tags": ["e35", "final", "n97", "window_closed", "inconclusive_threshold", "no_adoption", "best_powered"]}
